# Caribou Standard Parameters (PT1)
# Forked from Quiver standard-params.param (project-quiver
# docs/Operations/firmware/parameters/, PT3 base 2025-11-13) on 2026-07-20.
#
# Caribou deltas vs Quiver:
#   - FRAME_CLASS 1→2 (hexacopter, X layout)
#   - SERVO1..6 = Motor1..6. Per CMAIN_PCB schematics the FC main outputs
#     route IO_CH1→J27, IO_CH2→J32, IO_CH3→J40, IO_CH4→J23, IO_CH5→J45,
#     IO_CH6→J55 (4-pin JWPF ESC signal connectors, pin 4 = signal).
#     SERVOn ↔ IO_CHn ↔ that connector. ⚠ Wire each X15 ESC to the connector
#     matching its position in the ArduPilot HEXA/X motor diagram.
#   - ESC control = plain PWM (MOT_PWM_TYPE 10→0, CAN_D1_UC_ESC_BM 15→0):
#     CMAIN routes discrete PWM signal lines to the six ESC connectors,
#     Quiver's DroneCAN-ESC settings don't apply. ⚠ Confirm X15 input mode.
#   - Battery: 18S (Quiver was 14S) — all voltage thresholds rescaled at the
#     same per-cell setpoints. BATT_MONITOR 9(ESC)→8 (DroneCAN BatteryInfo,
#     to come from the CBCs once the CAN bridge fw is done). ⚠ Set
#     BATT_CAPACITY to the real Tattu 18S pack value.
#   - Obstacle avoidance / proximity stack removed (no RPLidar, no radar):
#     PRX1_*, RNGFND1_* gone, SERIAL5 lidar → -1, WPNAV_RFND_USE→0.
#     AVOID_ENABLE=0 / OA_TYPE=0 kept from base.
#   - Remote ID ENABLED (Quiver params-remoteid.param merged in, DID_* at
#     bottom). Assumes a DroneBeacon db201 on the DroneCAN bus like Quiver.
#   - SERVO_GPIO_MASK 65520→65472 (frees ch5+6 for motors, GPIO = ch7..16)
#
# ⚠⚠ TUNING PLACEHOLDERS — Quiver values, NOT valid for a ~200 kg hexa:
#   ATC_* PIDs/accels, MOT_THST_EXPO/SPIN_*, INS_HNTCH_* (notch freq 116 Hz
#   is Quiver's props; 63" props are much slower), LOIT/WPNAV speeds,
#   ANGLE_MAX, fence radius/alt. Retune before/at PT1 hover testing.
#
# ⚠ After loading, calibrate per-airframe:
#   - Compass (COMPASS_OFS_*, COMPASS_DIA_*, etc.)
#   - Accelerometer (INS_ACCOFFS_*, INS_ACCSCAL_*)
#   - RC (RC*_MIN, RC*_MAX, RC*_TRIM)
#   - Barometer (BARO*_GND_PRESS)

